      "content": "I can help you add a bit of flair to the email, while still keeping it professional and kind. Here's a revised draft:\n\n\"Dear [Candidate Name],\n\nI wanted to personally reach out to you regarding the status of your application for the Senior Developer position at [Company Name]. We were truly impressed by your technical skills and experience, particularly in cloud infrastructure, which aligns perfectly with our company's focus on scalability and innovation. Your expertise in this area was a major draw for us, and we were excited to explore how you could contribute to our team's efforts in this space.\n\nAfter careful consideration, we have decided to move forward with another candidate whose skills and experience align more closely with our current needs. Please know that this decision was not made lightly, and we were genuinely excited about the potential you brought to the table.\n\nI want to emphasize that this decision is in no way a reflection on your abilities or potential as a developer. You have a strong foundation, and I have no doubt that you will find a role that is a great fit for you.\n\nThank you again for your interest in joining our team, and I wish you all the best in your job search. We were particularly impressed by your passion for cloud infrastructure, and I",
